<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">25 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 25 August, from 325 to 2012.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">325</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The First Council of Nicaea closes</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">By tradition the council summoned by Constantine ended on this date. It had condemned Arianism, adopted the Nicene Creed and set rules for dating Easter, shaping Christian doctrine for centuries.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1609</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Galileo demonstrates his telescope to Venice's rulers</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Galileo showed the Venetian authorities his improved telescope, which made distant ships visible hours before they could be seen by eye. The Republic rewarded him with a lifetime post at Padua.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1825</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Uruguay declares independence from Brazil</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A congress at Florida declared the Banda Oriental independent of the Empire of Brazil and united with the River Plate provinces. After a war, Uruguay became a sovereign state under the 1828 treaty.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1919</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First daily international scheduled air service begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Aircraft Transport and Travel began daily flights between London's Hounslow Heath and Paris, carrying passengers, mail and goods. It was the start of scheduled international commercial aviation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1944</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Paris is liberated from German occupation</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">French and American troops entered Paris and the German commander, General von Choltitz, surrendered, having ignored Hitler's order to destroy the city. De Gaulle led a victory march the next day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">2012</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Neil Armstrong dies aged 82</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Neil Armstrong, the first person to walk on the Moon, died in Cincinnati after heart surgery. A modest engineer, he largely avoided the celebrity that followed Apollo 11.</p></li></ol>
